0, "launchWallSeconds": 2.094, "runIndex": 1, "textCheck": {"status": "PASS", "alphanumericCount": 907, "distinctWords": 108, "taskTerms": true, "flags": [], "method": "the runner's generated text (parsers: textExtraction) + lexical screen; full text retained"}, "textOutputSHA256": "92b9e809a5127d8ecc41c0726d760eb72601add1c4b4f743e065b41d92ab795d", "promptVersion": "noref-2026-10-19"}, "metrics": {"promptTokenCount": 1355, "generatedTokenCount": 255, "promptTokensPerSecond": 2920.2586206896553, "decodeTokensPerSecond": 212.5, "firstTokenLatencyMS": 464, "loadTimeSeconds": 0.251, "coldRun": true, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "initialThermalState": "nominal", "finalThermalState": "nominal", "memoryPeakResidentMB": 1323.015625}, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "decodedText": "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle this query. The user wants me to list 25 distinct things that on-device AI allows a phone to do that a cloud model can't. And each item needs two full sentences of explanation, numbered 0 to 24. They also mentioned not to stop early, so I need to make sure I cover all 25 points.\n\nFirst, I need to recall what on-device AI is. It's processing done on the device's hardware, not in the cloud. So, the phone can handle tasks without needing the cloud. That means things like real-time processing, lower latency, and more privacy. But I need to think of 25 specific things. Let me start brainstorming.\n\n1. Real-time processing: On-device AI can process data immediately, like image recognition or voice commands, without waiting for the cloud to respond. That's faster and more responsive.\n\n2. Reduced data transfer: Since the processing is done locally, less data needs to go to the cloud, which saves data usage and reduces network load.\n\n3. Lower latency: The device can process data instantly, which is better for time-sensitive tasks like voice commands or motion detection.\n\n4. Privacy: The data stays on the device, so it doesn", "outputSa